<p>			    NOTES TO FINANCIAL SUMMARIES</p>
<p>(1) Pro forma adjustments made in arriving at the estimated 1995 pro-forma data reflect Schweitzer-Mauduit's consolidated financial position and results of operations under certain assumptions, including the transactions contemplated in the spin-off and additional administrative and interest costs associated with operating as a separate, independent company, as if they had occurred as of the beginning of 1995.  Management believes these assumptions are reasonable.  The pro forma financial information is presented for informational purposes only and does not reflect the future earnings or results of operations of Schweitzer-Mauduit or what the earnings or results of operations of Schweitzer-Mauduit would have been had the predecessor operations been operated as a separate, independent company for the 1995 periods indicated.</p>
<p>(2) Certain reclassifications have been made to conform 1995 data to the current period presentation.</p>
<p>(3) A $7.3 million pre-tax restructuring charge, having an after-tax effect of $4.4 million ($0.27 net income per share), was recorded in the fourth quarter of 1995 as a result of the Company's decision to exit the reconstituted tobacco leaf product line in the U.S. and to restructure operations at the Malaucene, France mill.</p>
<p>(4) A French income tax rate increase from 33.33 percent to 36.67 percent was enacted in July 1995, retroactive to January 1, 1995. A one-time favorable impact on the deferred provision for income taxes of $4.5 million ($0.28 net income per share) was recorded in the third quarter 1995.  The unfavorable impact on the current provision for income taxes was $1.0 million for the nine-month period ended September 30, 1995 (including $0.6 million for a retroactive adjustment to the six-month period ended June 30, 1995) and an additional $0.3 million for the three-month period ended December 31, 1995.</p>
<p>(5) The average numbers of common shares outstanding for the quarter and year ended December 31, 1996 were approximately 16,052,600 and 16,052,100, respectively. The pro forma average number of common shares outstanding for both the quarter and year ended December 31, 1995 was approximately 16,051,100.</p>
